-- title:
--   The finite Type II estimate with coefficient 0.78
-- statement:
--   For the finite, odd-variable Vaughan bilinear sum with the centered logarithmic coefficient, assume the rational approximation and cutoff conditions in Tao's Theorem 5.1. Its norm is bounded by the explicit four-term logarithmic envelope with coefficients $0.1$, $0.39$, $0.55$, and $0.78$. The last two coefficients multiply $x/\sqrt U$ and $x/\sqrt V$, respectively.
-- source:
--   Terence Tao, Every odd number greater than 1 is the sum of at most five primes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6656, Sections 3 and 5. Original Lean source: Theorems/Thm_TaoFivePrimes_vaughan_typeII_bilinear_modulus_two_source.lean, lines 5-24.

